.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt FSCONF 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsconf
.Nd compiled file system table
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /boot/fsconf
is
.Pa /etc/fstab
in a form the kernel reads at boot, before it has mounted any file system, to
find the device that holds the root.
.Xr fsconf_mkdb 8
writes it; the boot loader loads it beside the kernel.
.Pp
All integers are little-endian.
The file is:
.Bl -enum
.It
the eight bytes
.Ql OXFSCONF ;
.It
a 32-bit version, 1;
.It
a 32-bit count of entries;
.It
that many entries, each four strings and two 32-bit integers: the device, the
mount point, the file system type and the options (comma-separated), each a
16-bit length followed by that many bytes of UTF-8; then the dump frequency
and the
.Xr fsck 8
pass number, as in
.Xr fstab 5 .
.El
.Pp
The kernel uses the entry for
.Pa / .
Its device is a partition of the data disk, by name
.Pq Pa /dev/virt0p1
or by GPT label
.Pq Pa /dev/gpt/rootfs .
If there is no
.Pa /boot/fsconf ,
or the device it names isn't on the disk, the kernel uses the disk's first oxfs
partition.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /boot/fsconf -compact
.It Pa /boot/fsconf
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr fsconf_mkdb 8
